{"content":[{"c":["HARROW*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Agricultural term for implement or procedure, though no implement corresponding to the modern harrow is known from Palestine or Egypt. ",{"href":"?bref=Job.39.10","r":"Job.39.10","rawR":"Job.39.10","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Job.39.10","value":"Job.39.10"}],"t":"ref","v":"Job 39:10"}," speaks of an ox performing the harrowing, while ",{"href":"?bref=Isa.28.24","r":"Isa.28.24","rawR":"Isa.28.24","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Isa.28.24","value":"Isa.28.24"}],"t":"ref","v":"Isaiah 28:24"}," notes that plowed ground was leveled as part of the process. Like the foregoing references, ",{"href":"?bref=Hos.10.11","r":"Hos.10.11","rawR":"Hos.10.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Hos.10.11","value":"Hos.10.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Hosea 10:11"}," speaks of harrowing in connection with plowing. Most probably harrowing consisted of branches being pulled behind an animal or plow to smooth the land and before seeding. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=Agriculture_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"Agriculture_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"Agriculture_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Agriculture"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Harrow","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Job 39:10","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Job.39.10","rawQueryValue":"Job.39.10","sourceRefExact":"Job.39.10"},{"anchorText":"Isaiah 28:24","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Isa.28.24","rawQueryValue":"Isa.28.24","sourceRefExact":"Isa.28.24"},{"anchorText":"Hosea 10:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Hos.10.11","rawQueryValue":"Hos.10.11","sourceRefExact":"Hos.10.11"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"aa40d996dd974d6a7515058b1964f83b75f49e22111f8409031dba935a05dd0e","sourceItemName":"Harrow","sourceItemOrder":128,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Harrow","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Harrow*","title":"Harrow*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}